les and blocking code","sub":"fs, spawn_blocking, DNS","short":"Files","main":"tokio::fs runs operations in a thread pool; blocking code goes to spawn_blocking.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["tokio::fs","spawn_blocking","DNS and Unix"],"captions":["File operations run in a thread pool; the interface is familiar","Heavy or blocking code goes to spawn_blocking: worker threads don't freeze","lookup_host resolves names; UnixListener — sockets at a file system path"],"frames":[[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":14.0,"lines":["fs::write(\"/tmp/a.txt\", b\"hi\").await?;","let s = fs::read_to_string(\"/tmp/a.txt\").await?;"],"hl":[0,1],"lang":"rust","size":9.0,"lh":18.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":14.0,"lines":["let h = tokio::task::spawn_blocking(|| {","    heavy_sum()         // blocking work","});","let v = h.await?;"],"hl":[0,1],"lang":"rust","size":9.5,"lh":16.0,"w":340.0}],[{"t":"code","id":"c","x":10.0,"y":14.0,"lines":["for a in lookup_host(\"example.org:443\").await? { … }","let l = UnixListener::bind(\"/tmp/s.sock\")?;"],"hl":[0,1],"lang":"rust","size":9.0,"lh":18.0,"w":340.0}]],"cues":[12.6,25.2]}]},{"title":"Summary","sub":"Networking in Tokio","short":"Summary","main":"Server: accept + spawn; client: connect; protocol: frames; timeouts everywhere.","body":[{"t":"scene","labels":["Server and client","Protocol","Next"],"captions":["accept + spawn on the server, connect on the client; read returned 0 — the end","TCP is a stream: needs frames; split, shutdown, UDP — as the task requires; timeouts everywhere","Next topic — cancellation, load and shutdown in a real application"],"frames":[[{"t":"cell","id":"a","x":65.0,"y":60.0,"w":110.0,"h":28.0,"text":"accept + spawn","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"b","x":180.0,"y":60.0,"w":110.0,"h":28.0,"text":"connect","tone":"green","size":10.0,"sub_size":8.5},{"t":"cell","id":"c","x":295.0,"y":60.0,"w":110.0,"h":28.0,"text":"read → 0 = EOF","tone":"green","size":9.5,"sub_size":